# E2E uploads use real data

An end-to-end upload sends a character to ENS (`roster register`) or puts an icon on the CDN. The input must be JSON written by `python -m roster propose` from a live Fandom `api.php` read.

- Do not pass `roster/fixtures/` or any other fixture file to `register` or to an icon upload.
- Do not hand-write `look` or `brief` for that run.
- Unit tests may keep saved API recordings and invented sheets. Those files must not be uploaded.
- If propose fails, stop. Do not substitute a fixture so the upload can continue.
